{title: 212 - 'Tis Almost Time for the Lord to Come}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #212 • TIS ALMOST TIME FOR THE  • 15.18.20.12}
{lyricist: G. W. Sederquist}
{composer: G. W. Sederquist}
{key: Db}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 212}
{meta: tune TIS ALMOST TIME FOR THE }
{meta: meter 15.18.20.12}
{meta: category Jesus Christ - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Db/F]'Tis almost time for the Lord [Bbm]to come, I hear [Ab7]the people say;
[Ab7]The stars of heavenare [Db/F]growing dim, It must be the breaking of the day.
[Db/Ab]O it must be the breaking [Ebm/Bb]of the day! O it must be [Bbm]the breaking of the day!
[Bbm]The night is [Db]almost gone, The day is coming on;
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Refrain}
[Db/Ab]O it must be the breaking [Ab]of the day!
[Ab]O it must be the [Db/Ab]breaking of the day!
[Db/Ab]The night is [Ab7]almost gone,
[Ab7]The day is coming [Ebm/Bb]on;
[Ebm/Bb]O it must be [Bbm]the breaking of the day!
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Db/F]The signs foretold [Bbm]in the sun [Ab7]and moon,
[Ab7]In earth [Db/F]and sea and sky,
[Db/Ab]Aloud proclaim [Ebm/Bb]to all [Bbm]mankind,
[Bbm]The coming [Db]of the Master draweth nigh.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Db/F]It must be time [Bbm]for the waiting [Ab7]church
[Ab7]To cast [Db/F]her pride away,
[Db/Ab]With girded [Ebm/Bb]loins and burning [Bbm]lamps,
[Bbm]To look [Db]for the breaking of the day.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[Db/F]Go quickly out in [Bbm]the streets and [Ab7]lanes
[Ab7]And in [Db/F]the broad highway,
[Db/Ab]And call the [Ebm/Bb]maimed, the halt, [Bbm]and blind,
[Bbm]To be ready [Db]for the breaking of the day.
{end_of_verse}
